              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Linda Costa"
            },
            "reviewBody": "WOW! I have a favorite dipping sauce that my husband and I like very much to use with coconut shrimp, but, this receipe as of dinner last night became our all time favorite.. however, I did not have stone-ground mustard instead I used dijon mustard.. then flavor was GREAT!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Challena"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I had to use Apricot Jam because I did not have orange. I doubled the recipe but only used 1 tsp of horseradish because the only kind in my frig was EXTRA HOT...which I use for cocktail sauce. I used combo of Dijon and Stoneground Brown mustard. It needed a little dash of sour for our taste and to cut the sweetness...so I put a teaspoon of key lime juice. I also think this would make an awesome ham glaze with some honey or brown sugar added to it.",
            "datePublished": "2012-04-06T09:49:22.773Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Gretchen"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I didn't have orange marmalade on hand,so I took a cup of orange juice and a large squirt of honey and reduced to half over medium heat, then added a corn starch slurry to thicken, then added the mustard and horse radish. It turned out great perfect with the baked coconut shrimp. Yum!!!!",
            "datePublished": "2017-09-07T22:19:52.750Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "babskitchen"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Really tasty and so easy to make. I did use regular mustard because I didn’t have stoneground or dijon. Mix a day in advance, if you can, so the flavors meld.",
            "datePublished": "2025-06-03T00:52:39.498Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
