            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Nasja1984"
            },
            "reviewBody": "i was surprised how good this was. i only had sugar free marmalade in the fridge at the time and I used that and it was very tasty. I added a bit of honey only because the marmalade had the 'sugar free bitter' taste.",
            "datePublished": "2019-04-06T20:07:24.343Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "VioletYeast4230"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Super super simple!! I did add more horsey sauce because I like a strong horseradish kick. And I plan on canning some of this so I always have it on hand!",
            "datePublished": "2024-10-10T17:36:30.601Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Brian"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Perfect pairing for \"Baked Coconut Shrimp\" on this site. I was a little concerned because I'm not a big fan of orange marmalade, but the stone ground mustard did a great job of toning down the sweet, and the horseradish brought a nice punch to go with all that sweet of coconut and marmalade. I did go a little heavy with the extra hot horseradish which worked for us that love the heat. Not generally an aesthetic guy, but the stone ground mustard did a nice job of toning down the bright orange. I'm sure dijon would work, but if you have the time, get the stone ground. Just a better flavor here.",
            "datePublished": "2015-02-16T09:21:39.070Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "missusdeeg"
            },
            "reviewBody": "We loved this! As well as the coconut shrimp recipe! This sauce was perfect although I had to tweek it bc I didn't have horseradish separately from mustard. What I have is a mustard with horseradish in it so I used same amount of orange marmalade and 2 tbs of the mustard. Delish!!!",
            "datePublished": "2014-04-19T19:05:27.907Z"
          },
